            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97045-golang.org/x/net",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-97045 medium vulnerability for golang.org/x/net package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In childTextNodesAreLiteral, walking up the tree previously stopped at the nearest foreign ancestor once an HTML integration point was found. However, that integration point may itself be a descendant of an element that was foster-parented into a foreign namespace (such as \u003cmglyph\u003e or \u003cmalignmark\u003e fostered under \u003cmtext\u003e), causing a parser to resolve the subtree in a different foreign namespace upon re-parsing the rendered output.\n\nContinue walking the full ancestor chain and verify that every transition from a non-empty namespace occurs at an HTML integration point before emitting literal text."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/855121",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97045\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: golang.org/x/net\nVersion: v0.0.0-20210226172049-e18ecbb05110\nFix Version: 0.62.0\nType: go-module\nLocation: /go.mod\nData Namespace: govulndb:language:go\nLink: [CVE-2026-97045](https://go.dev/cl/855121)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97045**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | golang.org/x/net  | v0.0.0-20210226172049-e18ecbb05110  | 0.62.0  | go-module  | /go.mod  | govulndb:language:go  | [CVE-2026-97045](https://go.dev/cl/855121)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/golang.org/x/net@v0.0.0-20210226172049-e18ecbb05110"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-25681-golang.org/x/net",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-25681 medium vulnerability for golang.org/x/net package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Parsing arbitrary HTML which is then rendered using Render can result in an unexpected HTML tree. This can be leveraged to execute XSS attacks in applications that attempt to sanitize input HTML before rendering."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/79574",
              "help": {
